ial-level issue because I don't  think anybody's gonna want to take it up  but I do think Rand Paul will be running  and I think he will talk about these  kinds of issues and he will get beat up  by the establishment conservative media  and all the other Republican candidates  and so it'll be interesting to see  whether he can hold up to all do you the  libertarian moment extending it into a  libertarian era or you know more than a  blip it doesn't really turn on whether  or not he's the Republican nominee or  not no that's right we're you know if  historical trends are bigger than any  one candidate now I think we can look  and see if Ronald Reagan had not been  the Republican nominee in 1980 would  things have been different probably so  so it does make a difference but  government programs will continue to  falter the economy will continue to  struggle because of the burdens placed  on it we will continue to get ourselves  involved in unnecessary wars the  president talked in State of the Union  speech about being dragged into  unnecessary conflicts of course he's  bomb seven countries and Bush only  bombed force or he should know but all  of these things will continue to be  problems and if Rand Paul doesn't get  elected president people may decide as  they did with Ronald Reagan boy we made  the wrong decision last time we should  vote for him next time or other  libertarian candidates will surely  emerge we've been talking with David  Bose he's the executive vice president  of the Cato Institute and the author  most recently of the new book the  libertarian mind of revised and updated  edition of libertarian as a primer it's  also subtitled of manifesto for freedom  David Bo's thanks for  thank you for reason TV I'm Nick  Gillespie
 

